What the message is telling you is that you are
passing

  matrix ~ normal(matrix,real[]),

or equivalently,

  normal_log(matrix, matrix, real[]).

This won't work. Only the signatures listed are available.
I'm not sure what your intent was with the statement with
matrix/matrix/real[] in terms of how the standard deviations
in the array line up with the means and outcomes in the two
matrices (and this is why we didn't choose to implement these
vectorizations!).

Marcus made a suggestion on how to deal with it, but I
thought I'd explain his reasoning.

- Bob

