Hi

I just want to make sure that I will be running 3 independent chains with the following code (I'm using Linux). Specifically, am I defining rng_seed OK?

library(parallel)
library(rstan)

setwd('~/ions/')

load('Co_data_oct16.dat')

foo <- stan(file = 'oct16.stan', data = datalist, chains=0)
rng_seed <-12345
sflist <- mclapply(
          1:3,
          mc.cores = 3,
           function(i) stan(fit = foo,
                            data = datalist,
                            iter=5000,
                            thin=5,
                            seed = rng_seed,
                            chains = 1,
                            chain_id = i,
                            refresh = -1))

modfit <- sflist2stanfit(sflist)

thanks

Mark

From u8aa9b8cc06fdc99c at groups.google.com  Fri Oct 17 16:14:44 2014
From: u8aa9b8cc06fdc99c at groups.google.com (Bob Carpenter)
Date: Fri, 17 Oct 2014 16:14:44 +0000
Subject: Re: [stan-users] Properly Running Chains in Parallel
Message-ID: <rLiOnCKMdVs.HNZOnWPl-CUJ@stan-users.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <rLiOnCKMdVs.ONPzADA3lfkJ@stan-users.groups.google.com>
References: <rLiOnCKMdVs.ONPzADA3lfkJ@stan-users.groups.google.com>
