Hi all,
I'm trying to speed up my model in Rstan and have been trying to move some calculations to the transformed parameters block, which I understand is a generally more efficient thing to do. However, when I do this, my model goes from running slowly to running REALLY slowly (i.e. I'm still waiting after 10 mins for it to perform one iteration). I'm completely stumped as to why this should be and would appreciate any pointers to help me understand what's happening:

Here is the first version of the model (no transformed parameters):

data{
int<lower=0> n;
int<lower=0> t;
vector[n] x;
vector[n] y;
vector[n] z;
int<lower=0> Rec[n];
int<lower=0> nWT;
int<lower=0> rec;
}

parameters{

real<lower=-1,upper=1> alpha[rec];
real<lower=0,upper=2> beta[rec];
