Hi Daniel

I am running on windows 7, this error happens on the R gui and also using it on Rstudio. As you say, I am using R and RTools without modification, the defaults

Something else that I found, is that it depends on which part of the code the error line is. To be clear, when the line is at the end of the model block (like my first example) the error doesnt show, like:

model{

corr_y ~ lkj_corr(1);
for(k in 1:nvars){
corr_b[k] ~ lkj_corr(1);}

for (j in 1:nsubj){
for (k in 1:nvars){

mu_b4[k] ~ normal(mub[k,4],var_mub4[k]);
b[k,j] ~ multi_normal_cholesky(mub[k], Lb[k]);
mub[k] ~ multi_normal_cholesky(pm[k], Lvb);
}}

for (i in 1:n){
y[i] ~ multi_normal_cholesky(mu[i], Ly);
mu[i] ~ multi_normal_cholesky(mm, Lvm);}

y_bio ~ normal(mu_bio, var_bio);
mu_bio ~ normal(mm_bio, 10);

for(j in 1:nsubj){
b_bio[j] ~ normal(mub_bio,varb_bio);}

for(k in 1:2){
mub_bio[k] ~ normal(0,10);}

reg ~ normal(0,50);
}

But, when the line reg ~ normal(0,50)  is before the part that sets the multinormal distributions (that gives the warnings for non linear transformation) the error does show the error for reg, like:

 model{

corr_y ~ lkj_corr(1);
for(k in 1:nvars){
corr_b[k] ~ lkj_corr(1);}

reg ~ normal(0,50);

for (j in 1:nsubj){
for (k in 1:nvars){

mu_b4[k] ~ normal(mub[k,4],var_mub4[k]);
b[k,j] ~ multi_normal_cholesky(mub[k], Lb[k]);
mub[k] ~ multi_normal_cholesky(pm[k], Lvb);
}}

for (i in 1:n){
y[i] ~ multi_normal_cholesky(mu[i], Ly);
mu[i] ~ multi_normal_cholesky(mm, Lvm);}

y_bio ~ normal(mu_bio, var_bio);
mu_bio ~ normal(mm_bio, 10);

for(j in 1:nsubj){
b_bio[j] ~ normal(mub_bio,varb_bio);}

for(k in 1:2){
mub_bio[k] ~ normal(0,10);}
}

Hope this helps to find out why this is happening

