On Monday, October 27, 2014 10:15:06 PM UTC-4, Xulong Wang wrote:
> So, why this takes so long, and are there ways to optimize this?

Bob explained why it can take a while. You might be able to squeeze some more speed out of it by exploiting the fact that the Cholesky factor is triangular. Something like

for(i in 1:N) {
  real temp;
  temp <- 0;
  for(j in 1:i) temp <- temp + CK[i,j] * z[j];
  u[i] <- temp;
}

Ben

